.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Data structure for a material\&. 

\fBMaterial\fP data is stored using a key-value structure\&. A single key-value pair is called a 'material property'\&. C++ users should use the provided member functions of \fBaiMaterial\fP to process material properties, C users have to stick with the aiMaterialGetXXX family of unbound functions\&. The library defines a set of standard keys (AI_MATKEY_XXX)\&. 
